        <tr><td><strong>🖥️ Presentation</strong></td><td>UI Console, n8n Proxy</td><td>User-facing interfaces. UI Console serves 23 EJS pages and proxies API calls to backend services. n8n Proxy strips security headers for iframe embedding.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong>⚙️ Application</strong></td><td>Agent Service, Tools Service, n8n</td><td>Core business logic. Agent Service runs the LangGraph ReAct loop, manages agents/skills/prompts/guardrails, and orchestrates LLM calls and tool execution. Tools Service provides a sandboxed runtime for untrusted operations. n8n handles visual workflow automation.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong>🧠 Intelligence</strong></td><td>Ollama, ChromaDB</td><td>AI inference and knowledge retrieval. Ollama serves local LLM models (llama3, mistral, phi3). ChromaDB stores document embeddings for RAG retrieval with cosine similarity search.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong>💾 Data</strong></td><td>SQLite, PostgreSQL</td><td>Persistent state. SQLite stores all platform configuration (agents, skills, prompts, guardrails, tools, A2A peers, MCP servers) plus conversation history and session summaries. PostgreSQL backs the Langfuse observability database.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong>📊 Observability</strong></td><td>OTel Collector, Prometheus, Grafana, Loki, Langfuse</td><td>Three-pipeline monitoring. Metrics (Prometheus), logs (Loki), and LLM traces (Langfuse) converge in Grafana dashboards. OTel Collector routes OTLP telemetry to the appropriate backends.</td></tr>
