      <p>The following sequence diagram shows a typical user interaction from prompt to streamed response, including memory loading, RAG retrieval, LLM inference, tool execution, and telemetry emission.</p>
      <div class="docs-diagram docs-diagram-full">
        <div class="mermaid">
sequenceDiagram
    participant U as 👤 User
    participant UI as 🖥️ UI Console<br/>(:3000)
    participant A as ⚙️ Agent Service<br/>(:8010)
    participant M as 💾 SQLite<br/>(memory.db)
    participant KB as 🧠 ChromaDB<br/>(:8200)
    participant LLM as 🧠 Ollama<br/>(:11436)
    participant T as ⚙️ Tools Service<br/>(:8011)
    participant OT as 📊 OTel + Langfuse

    U->>UI: Submit prompt
    UI->>A: POST /agent/run {message, session_id} (SSE)
    activate A
    A->>M: Load conversation history (STM)
    A->>M: Load session summary (LTM)
    A->>KB: Semantic search for relevant docs
    KB-->>A: Top-k document chunks
    Note over A: Build context:<br/>system prompt + memory +<br/>RAG chunks + guardrails
    A->>A: Run input guardrails (PII, injection, topic)
    A->>LLM: Chat completion (streaming)
    LLM-->>A: Stream tokens
    alt Tool call detected
        A->>T: POST /tools/{name} {args}
        T-->>A: Tool result (JSON)
        A->>LLM: Continue with tool results
        LLM-->>A: Final response stream
    end
    A->>A: Run output guardrails (toxicity, PII, length)
    A->>M: Save messages to conversations table
    A->>M: Update session summary (if threshold)
    A-->>OT: Emit OTLP span + Langfuse trace
    deactivate A
    A-->>UI: SSE stream (tokens)
    UI-->>U: Rendered markdown response
