      <h2>Inter-Service Communication</h2>
      <div class="docs-callout info">
        All inter-service calls use container DNS names (e.g. <code>http://agent-service:8000</code>, <code>http://ollama:11434</code>). Services never use <code>localhost</code> or host ports to reach each other. The only external dependency is the host network for user access.
      </div>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>UI → Agent:</strong> HTTP POST with SSE streaming for real-time responses</li>
        <li><strong>Agent → Tools:</strong> HTTP POST with JSON payloads for sandboxed tool execution</li>
        <li><strong>Agent → Ollama:</strong> OpenAI-compatible <code>/v1/chat/completions</code> API</li>
        <li><strong>Agent → ChromaDB:</strong> REST API for document embedding and similarity search</li>
        <li><strong>Agent → OTel:</strong> OTLP/gRPC on port 4317 for distributed tracing</li>
        <li><strong>Agent → Langfuse:</strong> Langfuse SDK for LLM-specific trace data</li>
        <li><strong>OTel → Prometheus:</strong> Remote-write metrics pipeline</li>
        <li><strong>OTel → Loki:</strong> Log forwarding pipeline</li>
        <li><strong>Langfuse → PostgreSQL:</strong> Standard <code>pg</code> connection for trace persistence</li>
      </ul>
